   "whatsnew": "a word your commands start with, such as copy, open or reset, now lists the commands that do it first, before components that only carry the word in their name: copy lists Copy op path above the CopyPars component. The palette learns these action words from the commands' own titles and help lines, so a new tool's commands teach it new ones. Every other word ranks as before. ships without the last search results from the authoring project. A typed word now also finds the words that mean the same in command titles: add and install, remove and delete, open, show and view, randomize, scramble and shuffle, restore and revert, quit and exit, create and new, load and import, and op, par and comp with their long forms and plurals. Those matches rank below the typed word itself and above help and docs hits.",
